**Problem.** At the Edgeville furnace the Varrock platebody bonus adds a free second bar (`outputBarCount` returns 2) and says "Your Varrock armour helps you smelt an extra <bar>." as a game message. On OSRS the platebody smelts the *next* ore at the same time, with the spam line "The Varrock platebody enabled you to smelt your next ore simultaneously.", sent before "You retrieve a bar of ...". RuneLite reads it that way:

- the Smelting plugin counts both lines as one bar each, `SPAM` only ([`SmeltingPlugin`](https://github.com/runelite/runelite/blob/master/runelite-client/src/main/java/net/runelite/client/plugins/smelting/SmeltingPlugin.java));
- the Item Charges plugin takes two ring of forging charges (one per iron ore) when "You retrieve a bar of iron." comes right after the platebody line ([`ItemChargePlugin`](https://github.com/runelite/runelite/blob/master/runelite-client/src/main/java/net/runelite/client/plugins/itemcharges/ItemChargePlugin.java), `RING_OF_FORGING_VARROCK_PLATEBODY` / `varrockPlatebodySmeltTwo`).

So the extra bar costs a second set of ores, and "You retrieve a bar of ..." is spam (it is a game message on main).

**Change.** In `SmeltingScript.performSmelt`:
- the ore removal moves into `consumeBarInputs`, used for the bar and, when the bonus rolls, for the next bar's ores (only if the player has them);
- both bars are added in one `invAdd`, each gives its XP, and both count towards the Make-X amount (`performSmelt` returns the number made);
- messages: the platebody line (if any), then "You retrieve a bar of ...", both `spam`.

The bonus conditions (Edgeville furnace, armour tier, the existing 10% roll, not for Superheat) are unchanged.

**Tests.** None added. Smelting has no test suite yet and the bonus roll uses `kotlin.random.Random` directly, so a test needs the roll injected (e.g. `GameRandom`); I can add that here if you'd like. Not checked in game on this branch.

**Caveats.** Inferred from the two messages and RuneLite's charge counting, not seen on live: that the bonus is skipped on the last bar of a Make-X (so it never makes more than asked), and that the second iron ore always refines (only the first one rolls the 50% iron failure without a ring of forging).

**Release note.** The Varrock platebody's extra bar at Edgeville now smelts the next ore at the same time (ores and XP for both bars), with the OSRS messages.

